    "created_at": "2025-10-08T18:04:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-08T18:04:12Z",
    "body": "https://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/ed05fb7007b0e8f5627781742986f457be6503a7#diff-41cf6794ba4200b839c53531555f0f3998df4cbb01a4d5cb0b94e3ca5e23947dR12185 - Initially in 2006 this was defined to have (in modern terms) an empty value default of True.\n\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/260c2c2b8b23e3e4524f1f7a4c5e44208f28e881 - but then in an update in 2007 during the definition of enumerated attributes the empty string aspect got lost from what I can see. As of this commit it's actually undefined what the invalid value default is but we can assume it became the Auto state implicitly.\n\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/0f1ee4bd965ea67fe7aabb2034fc0a5f95021dee - here in 2010 the examples got updated as they had still been using an empty value (which is part of why I think it was originally intended to have this behaviour)\n\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/7e941ae96b264d4743ea0afac00c3b3209ab0cde - much later in 2018 the invalid value default was explicitly defined as the Auto state.\n\n",
